@startuml
title Endless world: building, swapping and generating chunks
|worldBuilder|
start
:growAround(world, player cell);
:Walk rings 0..buildRadius (2) around the player's chunk,\nnearest first;
if (a missing chunk found?) then (no)
  :shrinkAround: chunks farther than keepRadius (3),\nfurthest first;
  |gameSerializer|
  :swapOutChunk: write elements of the chunk\nand what they carry to chunk_x_y.bin;
  :Remove them from the board;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
|worldBuilder|
if (chunk was swapped out before?) then (yes)
  |gameSerializer|
  if (swapInChunk reads chunk_x_y.bin?) then (yes)
    :Recreate the elements,\nre-link teleporters and apples;
    stop
  else (no)
  endif
endif
|randomLevelGenerator|
:generateChunk(start, patternFor(chunk));
:Seed from the world seed and the chunk;
:Lock the world mutex, batch teleporter registration;
:Fence: nothing may reach outside this chunk;
if (a pattern for this chunk?) then (yes)
  :fillChunk: place the pattern's elements,\ntiled from the top left cell;
  if (start chunk?) then (yes)
    :First pattern player is active,\nelse one on the floor nearest the middle;
  endif
else (no)
  :depth = difficulty::chunkDepth(chunk);
  :holes = difficulty::mazeHoles(depth);
  :buildMaze: spanning-tree maze of chamberAreas;
  :buildChunkWalls: west and north walls with gaps,\nopen the cell next to every gap;
  :placeEverything: monsters, bunkers, cameras,\nkeys, guns, apples, landmines, teleporters, doors\n(more danger with fewer holes);
endif
:Publish the batch of teleporters;
stop
@enduml
